  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hydro-powered Pumping Solutions for Farmers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gum acacia / gum Arabic is hardened sap from the acacia tree. Most of the gum is sourced in Sudan and used in many industries, such as confectionary, beverages, cosmetics and health. In current gum acacia trade, in average 11 steps are between farmer and manufacturer, while processing takes place outside of Sudan. Farmers live below the poverty line and their average age is high, while there is no return from the benefits in the chain. FOGA adds value at the start of the chain by removing the steps and is able to give farmers a fair price. FOGA Sudan built two factories for processing of the gum. A cleaning factory and a processing factory. A pre-financing loan for 3 containers of gum and will support workers in the factory as well as farmers.</narrative>
  </description>
